module ddpcrDetection
module rtddpcrDetection

manifest HEK293T_Cells
manifest TM_Buffer_01X
manifest ProximityProbe1_CD147
manifest ProximityProbe2_CD147
manifest ConnectorOligonucleotide
manifest LigationSolution
manifest ProteaseSolution
manifest ddPCR_Supermix_Probes
manifest UniversalPCRAssay
manifest CD147_TaqManAssay_Probe2
manifest GoScript_RT_System
manifest RandomPrimers
manifest dNTPs
manifest MgCl2
manifest RNaseOUT
manifest NucleaseFreeWater

// ============================================================
// Digital Quantification of Proteins and mRNA in Single
// Mammalian Cells.
// Albayrak, Jordi, Zechner, Lin, Bichsel, Khammash, Tay.
// Molecular Cell 61, 914-924, March 17, 2016.
// DOI: http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.molcel.2016.02.030
//
// This BioScript file encodes the joint single-cell protein
// (digital PLA) and mRNA (two-step RT-ddPCR) quantification
// workflow for CD147 from single HEK293T cells.
//
// WORKFLOW OVERVIEW:
//   1. Single HEK293T cell is FACS-sorted into 3 uL of 0.1X
//      TM lysis buffer.
//   2. Lysate is split 1:2 -> 1 uL for mRNA (RT-ddPCR),
//      2 uL for protein (digital PLA).
//   3. Digital PLA arm: proximity probes bind CD147 protein;
//      connector oligonucleotide hybridises; ligation forms
//      dsDNA; protease digestion removes antibodies; dsDNA
//      quantified by ddPCR in 20,000 nanoliter droplets.
//   4. RT-ddPCR arm: two-step RT (GoScript at 42 C, 1 hr)
//      followed by ddPCR (40 cycles, 60 C annealing) using
//      TaqMan Probe 2 (Hs00174305_m1).
//   5. QC gates on both ddPCR readouts; results disposed or
//      drained accordingly.
//
// NOTE ON LYSATE SPLIT ABSTRACTION:
//   BioScript has no native split-by-ratio operator.
//   The 1 uL mRNA fraction and 2 uL protein fraction are
//   modelled as two independent dispense events from the same
//   manifest (TM_Buffer_01X used as the lysis carrier), each
//   representing the respective volume fraction of a single
//   lysed cell. This is consistent with the abstraction
//   pattern used in the reference .bs files for similar
//   multi-fraction workflows.
//
// NOTE ON TEMPERATURE / TIME TOKENS:
//   BioScript `heat` accepts temperatures in degrees C (e.g.
//   37c) and durations in seconds (s) or minutes (m).
//   All times are converted accordingly:
//     60 min probe adsorption  -> 60m
//     10 min ligation          -> 10m
//     10 min protease          -> 10m
//     15 min protease inact.   -> 15m
//      5 min primer annealing  ->  5m
//     60 min reverse transcript-> 60m
//     15 min RT inactivation   -> 15m
//     PCR cycling abstracted as heat step (40 cycles ~35 min) -> 35m
//
// NOTE ON ddPCR CYCLE ABSTRACTION:
//   40 PCR amplification cycles at 94 C/60 C are modelled as
//   a single `heat` step at 94c for 35m (approximate total
//   cycling time). The subsequent 98 C 10 min final extension
//   is modelled as heat at 98c for 10m. The initial 95 C 10
//   min hot-start is heat at 95c for 10m.
//
// NOTE ON MODULE SCOPE:
//   ddpcrDetection  -> digital PLA protein readout (counts
//                      dsDNA amplicons per uL, converted to
//                      protein copy numbers via calibration).
//   rtddpcrDetection -> RT-ddPCR mRNA readout (counts cDNA
//                       amplicons per uL, corrected for 87.6%
//                       RT recovery rate, reported as mRNA
//                       copies per cell).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main           -- entry: cell lysis, lysate split,
//                          digital PLA arm, RT-ddPCR arm
//   BB2  proteinPass    -- proteinSignal > 0: CD147 protein
//                          detected above LOD (29,300 mol/cell
//                          in 2 uL fraction); dispose
//   BB3  proteinFail    -- proteinSignal <= 0: below LOD; drain
//   BB4  proteinJoin    -- join: mRNA QC gate follows
//   BB5  mRNAPass       -- mRNASignal > 0: CD147 mRNA detected
//                          above LOD (52.5 copies/cell); dispose
//   BB6  mRNAFail       -- mRNASignal <= 0: below LOD; drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup   -- terminal: dispose QC signals; end
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: FACS sort single HEK293T cell into 3 uL of 0.1X
//         TM lysis buffer.
//         DRAQ7 nuclear dye used to gate viable cells.
//         Tlr4-GFP expression used as sort marker (R4 gate).
//         Plate sealed immediately after sort and stored
//         at -80 C until processing.
//         `mix` here abstracts the sort-and-lyse event;
//         the cell contacts 0.1X TM buffer in the well,
//         releasing intracellular contents (protein + mRNA).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cellLysate     = dispense 1 units of TM_Buffer_01X
sortedCell     = dispense 1 units of HEK293T_Cells
lysate         = mix sortedCell with cellLysate for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Split lysate into two fractions.
//         PROTEIN FRACTION (2/3 of lysate -> 2 uL):
//           carried into the digital PLA arm below.
//         mRNA FRACTION (1/3 of lysate -> 1 uL):
//           carried into the RT-ddPCR arm below.
//
//         BioScript abstraction: two independent variables
//         derived from the same lysate represent the two
//         physical fractions. No array split is used (see
//         note on compiler constraint above).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Protein fraction (2 uL) -- modelled as primary lysate
proteinFraction = dispense 2 units of TM_Buffer_01X
proteinLysate   = mix lysate with proteinFraction for 5s

// mRNA fraction (1 uL) -- modelled as secondary lysate
mRNAFraction    = dispense 1 units of TM_Buffer_01X
mRNALysate      = mix lysate with mRNAFraction for 5s

// ============================================================
// DIGITAL PLA ARM (CD147 Protein Quantification)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Proximity probe adsorption.
//         2 uL protein lysate + 2 uL probe solution
//         (400 pM each proximity probe -> 200 pM final).
//         Proximity probe 1 and probe 2 are pre-mixed into
//         a single assay probe solution; both recognise
//         distinct epitopes of CD147 simultaneously.
//         Incubated at 37 C for 60 min (probe adsorption).
//
//         When both probes bind the same CD147 molecule,
//         their tethered oligonucleotides come into close
//         proximity (~40 nm) enabling connector hybridisation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probesSolution  = dispense 1 units of ProximityProbe1_CD147
probe2Disp      = dispense 1 units of ProximityProbe2_CD147
probesMix       = mix probesSolution with probe2Disp for 5s

probeBindingRxn = mix proteinLysate with probesMix for 60m
heat probeBindingRxn at 37c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Connector oligonucleotide hybridisation and ligation.
//         96 uL ligation solution (containing connector oligo,
//         ligase, and ligation buffer) added to the 4 uL
//         probe-bound sample -> 25-fold dilution.
//         The connector oligonucleotide hybridises to the
//         paired probe oligonucleotides, and T4 DNA ligase
//         seals the nicks, forming a dsDNA molecule encoding
//         the protein detection event.
//         Incubated at 37 C for 10 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

connectorOligo  = dispense 1 units of ConnectorOligonucleotide
ligationSoln    = dispense 1 units of LigationSolution
ligationPrep    = mix connectorOligo with ligationSoln for 5s

ligationRxn     = mix probeBindingRxn with ligationPrep for 10m
heat ligationRxn at 37c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Protease digestion to remove antibody-oligonucleotide
//         conjugates.
//         2 uL diluted protease solution added to ligation mix.
//         Incubated at 37 C for 10 min to digest antibodies,
//         leaving only the dsDNA amplicons in solution.
//         Protease inactivated at 95 C for 15 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

proteaseDisp    = dispense 1 units of ProteaseSolution
afterProtease   = mix ligationRxn with proteaseDisp for 10m
heat afterProtease at 37c for 10m
heat afterProtease at 95c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: ddPCR droplet generation and amplification.
//         9 uL of PLA solution + 10 uL 2X ddPCR Supermix for
//         Probes + 1 uL 20X Universal PCR Assay -> 20 uL total.
//         Emulsified by QX100 Droplet Generator into ~20,000
//         nanoliter droplets (~0.85 nL each) at limiting
//         dilution (each droplet contains 0 or 1 dsDNA).
//
//         PCR temperature schedule:
//           95 C for 10 min (hot-start activation)
//           40 cycles: 94 C 30 s / 60 C 1 min
//           98 C for 10 min (final denaturation)
//         Ramp speed: 2.5 C/s.
//
//         Fluorescence read on QX100 Droplet Reader;
//         QuantaSoft v1.3.2.0 converts positive/negative
//         droplet counts to DNA concentration using Poisson
//         statistics: C = (1000/Vd) * ln(1 - P/R).
//         Absolute protein counts derived via calibration curve
//         (CD147: y = 0.0142x + 12.4, R2 = 0.9997;
//          LOD = 86 proteins/uL ddPCR solution = 16.2 fM;
//          sensitivity = 70 proteins per DNA count).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ddpcrSupermix   = dispense 1 units of ddPCR_Supermix_Probes
universalPCR    = dispense 1 units of UniversalPCRAssay
ddpcrMix        = mix ddpcrSupermix with universalPCR for 5s
plasDdpcrRxn    = mix afterProtease with ddpcrMix for 5s

// Hot-start activation
heat plasDdpcrRxn at 95c for 10m

// 40 amplification cycles (94 C 30s / 60 C 1 min; ~35 min total)
heat plasDdpcrRxn at 94c for 35m

// Final denaturation / signal stabilisation
heat plasDdpcrRxn at 98c for 10m

// Detect: ddPCR droplet fluorescence readout
// ddpcrDetection module abstracts QX100 reader + QuantaSoft
// concentration calculation and calibration curve conversion.
proteinSignal   = detect ddpcrDetection on plasDdpcrRxn for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Protein QC gate
// Pass (BB2): proteinSignal > 0 -> CD147 protein detected
//             above assay LOD (29,300 molecules/cell in 2 uL
//             fraction after 113-fold dilution in workflow);
//             dispose processed PLA solution.
// Fail (BB3): proteinSignal <= 0 -> below LOD; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (proteinJoin).
// ============================================================

if (proteinSignal > 0) {
    dispose plasDdpcrRxn
} else {
    drain plasDdpcrRxn
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: proteinJoin
// Dispose protein QC signal. Control falls into
// the RT-ddPCR mRNA quantification arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose proteinSignal

// ============================================================
// RT-ddPCR ARM (CD147 mRNA Quantification)
// Two-step protocol: GoScript RT followed by ddPCR.
// TaqMan Gene Expression Assay Hs00174305_m1 (Probe 2).
// 40 amplification cycles.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Primer annealing for reverse transcription.
//         1 uL mRNA lysate + 1 uL random primer solution
//         + nuclease-free water to 4.95 uL.
//         Incubated at 70 C for 5 min (denature RNA secondary
//         structure), then immediately chilled on ice for 5 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

randomPrimersDisp  = dispense 1 units of RandomPrimers
waterDisp          = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
primerAnnealMix    = mix mRNALysate with randomPrimersDisp for 5s
primerAnnealFull   = mix primerAnnealMix with waterDisp for 5s

// Denaturation at 70 C for 5 min
heat primerAnnealFull at 70c for 5m

// Ice chilling: modelled as 4 C for 5 min
heat primerAnnealFull at 4c for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Reverse transcription master mix assembly.
//         GoScript Reverse Transcription System:
//           1X GoScript reaction buffer
//           GoScript RT (1/20 dilution from stock)
//           1 U/uL RNaseOUT ribonuclease inhibitor
//           0.5 mM each dNTP
//           3.1 mM MgCl2
//         Final RT volume: 9 uL.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

goScriptRT      = dispense 1 units of GoScript_RT_System
rnaseOut        = dispense 1 units of RNaseOUT
dntpsDisp       = dispense 1 units of dNTPs
mgcl2Disp       = dispense 1 units of MgCl2

rtBufferMix     = mix goScriptRT with rnaseOut for 5s
rtReagentsMix   = mix rtBufferMix with dntpsDisp for 5s
rtMasterMix     = mix rtReagentsMix with mgcl2Disp for 5s

rtFullRxn       = mix primerAnnealFull with rtMasterMix for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Two-step reverse transcription.
//         Step A: 25 C for 5 min (random primer annealing).
//         Step B: 42 C for 60 min (cDNA synthesis).
//         Step C: 70 C for 15 min (RT inactivation).
//
//         Expected recovery: 87.6% of theoretical CD147 mRNA
//         signal (measured against T7 in-vitro transcribed
//         CD147 mRNA standard at A260). All single-cell
//         RT-ddPCR reads corrected by this recovery rate.
//         Corrected LOD: 52.5 copies/cell (87 aM).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Step A: primer annealing
heat rtFullRxn at 25c for 5m

// Step B: cDNA synthesis
heat rtFullRxn at 42c for 60m

// Step C: RT enzyme inactivation
heat rtFullRxn at 70c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: ddPCR of cDNA.
//          cDNA solution + 10 uL 2X ddPCR Supermix for Probes
//          + 1 uL 20X CD147 TaqMan Gene Expression Assay
//          (Probe 2, Hs00174305_m1; FAM/MGB; spanning
//          exon-exon junction to exclude genomic DNA).
//          Final volume: 20 uL.
//          Emulsified -> ~20,000 droplets.
//
//          PCR temperature schedule:
//            95 C for 10 min (hot-start)
//            40 cycles: 94 C 30 s / 60 C 1 min
//            98 C for 10 min (final denaturation)
//          Ramp speed: 2.5 C/s.
//
//          Positive/negative droplets counted by QX100.
//          DNA concentration: C = (1000/Vd) * ln(1 - P/R).
//          mRNA copies per cell = C * volume * (1/recovery_rate)
//          where recovery_rate = 0.876 (87.6%).
//          Expected: mean 188.2 +/- 90 CD147 mRNA copies/cell.
//          Fluorescence threshold: 3200 RFU (Probe 2, 40 cycles).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ddpcrSupermix2  = dispense 1 units of ddPCR_Supermix_Probes
taqmanProbe2    = dispense 1 units of CD147_TaqManAssay_Probe2
rtDdpcrMix      = mix ddpcrSupermix2 with taqmanProbe2 for 5s
rtDdpcrRxn      = mix rtFullRxn with rtDdpcrMix for 5s

// Hot-start activation
heat rtDdpcrRxn at 95c for 10m

// 40 amplification cycles (~35 min total for 94 C/60 C cycling)
heat rtDdpcrRxn at 94c for 35m

// Final denaturation
heat rtDdpcrRxn at 98c for 10m

// Detect: RT-ddPCR droplet fluorescence readout
// rtddpcrDetection module abstracts QX100 reader + QuantaSoft
// mRNA copy number calculation + 87.6% RT recovery correction.
mRNASignal      = detect rtddpcrDetection on rtDdpcrRxn for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: mRNA QC gate
// Pass (BB5): mRNASignal > 0 -> CD147 mRNA detected above
//             corrected LOD (52.5 copies/cell = 87 aM);
//             dispose processed RT-ddPCR solution.
// Fail (BB6): mRNASignal <= 0 -> below LOD; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (mRNASignal > 0) {
    dispose rtDdpcrRxn
} else {
    drain rtDdpcrRxn
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose both QC signal droplets. Experiment ends.
// Protein and mRNA copy numbers are now available for:
//   - Spearman correlation analysis (rho = 0.10 across cells)
//   - Gamma distribution fitting to mRNA distribution
//   - Stochastic two-state model parameterisation via
//     moment-based MCMC inference (Zechner et al., 2012)
//   - Transcription burst size (~40 mRNA/burst), burst rate
//     (3.78/day), translation ratio (~1000 proteins/mRNA)
// ============================================================

dispose mRNASignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
